      "side": 1,
      "message": "In your four USB transfer functions (`IapSendCommand`, `IapRecvStatus`, `IapSendData`, `IapRecvData`), you are casting `buff.size()` to an `int` twice per function—once for the `libusb` call and once for the validation check.\n\nYou can halve the number of casts by storing the integer size upfront.\n\n**Instead of this:**\n\n```cpp\n  err_code \u003d libusb_interrupt_transfer(\n      dev_handle_ptr_.get(), ep_out, const_cast\u003cunsigned char *\u003e(buff.data()),\n      static_cast\u003cint\u003e(buff.size()), \u0026transferred, kTimeoutTransferMs);\n  // ...\n  if (transferred !\u003d static_cast\u003cint\u003e(buff.size())) {\n\n```\n\n**Do this:**\n\n```cpp\n  const int transfer_len \u003d static_cast\u003cint\u003e(buff.size());\n  \n  err_code \u003d libusb_interrupt_transfer(\n      dev_handle_ptr_.get(), ep_out, const_cast\u003cuint8_t*\u003e(buff.data()),\n      transfer_len, \u0026transferred, kTimeoutTransferMs);\n  // ...\n  if (transferred !\u003d transfer_len) {\n\n```\n\n*(Note: I also changed `unsigned char *` to `uint8_t*` in the `const_cast`, as `uint8_t` is universally an alias for `unsigned char` and matches your span\u0027s type perfectly).*",
